# libpdx-unicode-tables -- collation fingerprint golden
#
# Format: tab-separated `TAG\tOP\tA_HEX\tB_HEX\tOUTPUT_HEX`.
#
#   OP in {CMP, KEY}.
#
#   For CMP: A_HEX and B_HEX are the two input byte strings (as hex, no
#   spaces); OUTPUT_HEX is the i64 return value of _coll_compare encoded
#   as a 64-bit unsigned hex pattern:
#     -1 -> FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
#      0 -> 0000000000000000
#     +1 -> 0000000000000001
#
#   For KEY: A_HEX is the single input byte string; B_HEX is the `-`
#   placeholder (no second input); OUTPUT_HEX is the materialised UCA
#   sort key as the exact byte sequence _coll_sort_key writes to the
#   output buffer, encoded as hex (no spaces).  An empty key is the
#   literal `-` placeholder (both HEX columns and the OUTPUT column
#   can be `-`), so trailing-tab stripping by any editor cannot elide
#   a semantic value: the driver's parser recognises `-` as "no bytes".
#
# Reduced DUCET baseline (R131.M4):
#
#   * ASCII printable U+0020..U+007E -- space/punct/digit/letter bands.
#   * Latin-1 combining mark U+0301 (ACUTE) L2 = 0x0024.
#   * Non-decomposing Latin-1 / Latin-Ext-A cps fall into fallback bands
#     strictly above ASCII letters.  (None of the fingerprints below
#     exercise fallback cps.)
#
# CE weight constants (match src/collation.pdx SECTION 3):
#   L1(lowercase ASCII a..z) = 0x1C00 + (cp - 0x61) * 4
#                              i.e. 'a'=0x1C00, 'b'=0x1C04, 'c'=0x1C08,
#                                   'e'=0x1C10, 'f'=0x1C14
#   L1(uppercase ASCII A..Z) = 0x1C00 + (cp - 0x41) * 4
#                              i.e. 'A'=0x1C00 (same L1 as 'a')
#   L2(base letter)          = 0x0020
#   L2(U+0301 acute)         = 0x0024
#   L3(lowercase, mark)      = 0x0002
#   L3(uppercase)            = 0x0008
#
# Sort-key layout per CE pass:
#   level-1 bytes (big-endian u16 per non-zero L1 weight), then 00 00
#   level-2 bytes (big-endian u16 per non-zero L2 weight), then 00 00
#   level-3 bytes (big-endian u16 per non-zero L3 weight), NO trailing sep.
#
# Milestone: M4 (paideia-os#2615, R131.M4).
#
# Case walk-through (manual):
#
#   KEY_a: NFD('a') = 'a'. CE = (L1=0x1C00, L2=0x0020, L3=0x0002).
#          L1 stream = 1C 00; sep = 00 00; L2 stream = 00 20; sep = 00 00;
#          L3 stream = 00 02.  Total 10 bytes:
#              1C 00 00 00 00 20 00 00 00 02   (hex: 1C000000002000000002)
#
#   CMP_AB: Key('a') = 1C 00 00 00 00 20 00 00 00 02 (10 B).
#           Key('b') = 1C 04 00 00 00 20 00 00 00 02 (10 B).
#           Byte 1: 0x00 < 0x04 -> 'a' < 'b' -> -1.
#
#   CMP_a_vs_A: Key('a') ends ... 00 02; Key('A') ends ... 00 08.
#               Byte 9: 0x02 < 0x08 -> 'a' < 'A' -> -1 (lower < upper, L3).
#
#   CMP_a_vs_aacute: NFD('á') = 'a' + U+0301. CEs:
#                      (0x1C00, 0x0020, 0x0002), (0, 0x0024, 0x0002).
#                    Key('á') L1 = 1C 00 (mark L1=0 skipped);
#                             L2 = 00 20 00 24;
#                             L3 = 00 02 00 02.  Total 14 bytes:
#                      1C 00 00 00 00 20 00 24 00 00 00 02 00 02
#                    Key('a') diverges from Key('á') at byte 6 where
#                    'a' has 00 (continuing separator) vs 'á' has 00
#                    (fine, continue) ... then byte 7: 'a' has 00 vs
#                    'á' has 24 -> 'a' < 'á' -> -1.
#
#   CMP_cafe_vs_café: Same shape as a_vs_aacute but longer prefix.
#                     The acute mark on the final 'e' pushes 'café'
#                     past 'cafe' at the L2-stream separator byte.

CMP_AB	CMP	61	62	FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
CMP_BA	CMP	62	61	0000000000000001
CMP_AA	CMP	61	61	0000000000000000
CMP_a_vs_A	CMP	61	41	FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
CMP_a_vs_aacute	CMP	61	C3A1	FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
CMP_cafe_vs_café	CMP	63616665	636166C3A9	FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
KEY_a	KEY	61	-	1C000000002000000002
KEY_empty	KEY	-	-	-
